# UPLAA-412 — block public download of un-watermarked full-resolution store masters.
#
# The /shop/ photo products expose an un-watermarked "-master-<hex>" attachment
# whose bare/large renditions are directly downloadable by URL (strip the size
# suffix), leaking the sellable full-res original. This lives in wp-content/
# (not uploads/) on purpose: the site-deploy rsync EXCLUDES uploads/, but a
# <FilesMatch> in wp-content/ cascades to every file under wp-content/uploads/.
#
# Scope is surgical: rules ONLY match the "-master-<hex>" stem. The watermarked
# product-display images (<slug>.jpg, e.g. 001-city-idaho-falls*.jpg — NO
# "-master-" stem) that power the product image + zoom/lightbox are never
# matched, and the small square thumbnails the store actually shows from the
# master (-100x100 gallery-nav, -300x300 shop-grid/related) are explicitly
# re-allowed below. Reversible: delete this file / revert the commit.

# 1) Deny every rendition of the un-watermarked master (bare full-res original,
#    -scaled, and all -WxH renditions). None of these are displayed anywhere.
<FilesMatch "-master-[0-9a-f]+(-[0-9]+x[0-9]+|-scaled)?\.(jpe?g|png|webp)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# 2) Re-allow ONLY the small square thumbnails the store genuinely displays:
#    -300x300 (shop grid + related products) and -100x100 (gallery nav strip).
#    Listed AFTER the deny so the grant wins for these two sizes (Apache 2.4
#    merges matching <FilesMatch> in order; last match wins).
<FilesMatch "-master-[0-9a-f]+-(100x100|300x300)\.(jpe?g|png|webp)$">
    Require all granted
</FilesMatch>

# 3) UPLAA-418 — re-allow ONLY the 768x432 web rendition of the FIVE cleared,
#    watermark-free aerials that the public /drone-services/ gallery displays
#    (Code Snippet 108 renders the collection tiles from the master's
#    "medium_large" = 768x432). These five source files are intentionally public
#    marketing imagery (UPLAA-159 / UPLAA-201 / UPLAA-217); their 403 was
#    collateral from Rule 1, not intended confidentiality.
#
#    Scoped to the exact five master hashes AND only the 768x432 size, so the
#    store deny stays airtight everywhere else: every OTHER master is still
#    fully denied, and for these five the bare original, -scaled, and all larger
#    renditions (1024x576, 1536x864, 2048x…) remain denied by Rule 1. Nothing
#    sellable is exposed — 768x432 is a low-res web preview, not a deliverable.
#      010-city-idaho-falls        -> 59481200e0bb577f
#      030-city-pocatello          -> e204f40adcc85108
#      035-city-kaysville          -> a2e0e6a5dc65a469
#      039-city-soda-springs       -> d483a1839446c48b
#      123-moun-palisades-reservoir-> ac2db056a2191d4b
<FilesMatch "-master-(59481200e0bb577f|e204f40adcc85108|a2e0e6a5dc65a469|d483a1839446c48b|ac2db056a2191d4b)-768x432\.(jpe?g|png|webp)$">
    Require all granted
</FilesMatch>
